# What the build makes
/_output/*
/_models/*
_docs/
_docs_src/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

# A real project COMMITS chartbook.lock. It is what says which data the
# project was built against, and a change to it should show up in a diff.
#
# This example cannot. Its upstream, ../yield_curve, pulls live data, so the
# bytes it depends on are different on every build, and a committed lockfile
# would name data that no clone could get back.
chartbook.lock
